  "worked_solution": "The matrix of our system is\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that:\n\n- Since the only (repeated) eigenvalue of $A$ is $\\lambda =3$ and it's positive, we have a $\\text{unstable}$ node.\n\n- Since $A$ is diagonal and has a repeated eigenvalue, there are infinitely many linearly independent eigenvectors. So, we have a $\\text{star}$ node.\n\n**Note:** The phase portrait of the system looks as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14124655/assets/95bb5be106524711e86d2e1ff9cb21d61141c25eb0a2f8958b51c29791806ccc.png)",
